# ⛔ Hashed files must be byte-identical on every platform.
#
# manifest.json records a SHA-256 of each text.md. If git converts line endings on
# checkout, a clone on Windows produces different bytes than the hash recorded on
# Linux — and every acceptance record that cites that hash stops verifying.
#
# `-text` disables EOL conversion entirely: the bytes committed are the bytes checked
# out, everywhere. Do not "tidy" this into `text eol=lf`; that still normalises.
licences/**/text.md   -text
manifest.json         -text

# The rest may normalise; nothing hashes it.
*.md                  text
*.mjs                 text
*.json                text
